1
00:02:50,280 --> 00:02:53,360
No, please. I'm scared.

2
00:02:55,160 --> 00:02:56,439
Please don't.

3
00:02:56,440 --> 00:02:58,040
What is it?

4
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:01,880
Could it be Sairung, Mr. Phum's wife?

5
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:04,360
If you come any closer,

6
00:03:05,120 --> 00:03:06,320
I'll shoot.

7
00:03:08,480 --> 00:03:09,600
Kaimook!

8
00:03:15,720 --> 00:03:17,920
Thon, calm down.

9
00:03:18,880 --> 00:03:20,360
Kaimook is smart.

10
00:03:20,960 --> 00:03:23,000
I'm sure she'll find a way.

11
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:41,080
What are you going to do with this woman?

12
00:03:44,440 --> 00:03:45,720
Drag her out

13
00:03:46,440 --> 00:03:47,800
and get rid of her.

14
00:03:51,600 --> 00:03:52,720
Are you sure?

15
00:03:53,320 --> 00:03:55,040
Or are you going to let her go
to the police?

16
00:03:56,160 --> 00:03:57,920
It's not like
you've never killed anyone before.

17
00:04:01,240 --> 00:04:02,640
Are you scared?

18
00:04:38,400 --> 00:04:39,440
Get down here.

19
00:04:43,680 --> 00:04:44,960
Where are you taking me?

20
00:04:49,200 --> 00:04:50,120
Just come with me.

21
00:04:51,640 --> 00:04:53,600
- No. Let me go.
- Come on.

22
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:56,280
- Please let me go! Don't hurt me!
- Stop talking. Come here.

23
00:05:00,800 --> 00:05:02,759
Let me go.

24
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:05,159
Help me!

25
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:06,720
Go.

26
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:09,079
Help me.

27
00:05:09,080 --> 00:05:10,239
Those two.

28
00:05:10,240 --> 00:05:11,800
They're trying to hurt me.

29
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:25,639
Mr. Phum.

30
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:27,999
Mr. Narathon. What happened?

31
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:29,800
Stop asking. Untie us. Quickly!

32
00:05:40,080 --> 00:05:41,120
Kaimook.

33
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:44,520
Hello, Kaimook?

34
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:46,720
Where are you?

35
00:05:47,440 --> 00:05:48,480
Okay.

36
00:05:49,400 --> 00:05:50,440
Alright.

37
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:52,560
What did she say?

38
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:57,480
She got away.

39
00:05:58,600 --> 00:06:00,159
She's on her way back

40
00:06:00,160 --> 00:06:01,600
and she told us to wait here.

41
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,119
Are you going to call the police?

42
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:05,320
No.

43
00:06:06,080 --> 00:06:07,680
I'll handle this myself.

44
00:06:09,360 --> 00:06:10,959
Sairung can't have gotten very far.

45
00:06:10,960 --> 00:06:12,000
Trust me.

46
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:37,080
- Damn it!
- What happened?

47
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:38,679
My cards.

48
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:40,240
None of them work.

49
00:06:40,960 --> 00:06:41,960
Is the machine broken?

50
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:44,279
Broken my ass.

51
00:06:44,280 --> 00:06:45,680
All my cards have been frozen.

52
00:06:46,720 --> 00:06:48,160
It has to be Mr. Phum's doing.

53
00:06:48,880 --> 00:06:50,959
He thinks he can corner me?

54
00:06:50,960 --> 00:06:52,120
No way.

55
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:55,080
Without money, we can't go anywhere.

56
00:06:57,240 --> 00:06:59,559
I still have some jewelry.
Take it and sell it.

57
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:00,760
Where is it?

58
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:03,120
In the suitcase.

59
00:07:06,080 --> 00:07:07,720
I forgot it at home!

60
00:07:08,840 --> 00:07:10,960
Why did this happen to me?

61
00:07:12,120 --> 00:07:14,120
How am I supposed to run away
without any money?

62
00:07:19,680 --> 00:07:20,919
Hey.

63
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:22,360
Calm down.

64
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:24,960
I know a place

65
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:26,999
where we can stay

66
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,400
even without money.

67
00:07:29,320 --> 00:07:30,360
Where?

68
00:07:32,080 --> 00:07:33,720
Just drive. I'll tell you the way.

69
00:07:53,920 --> 00:07:54,760
Thon.

70
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:57,040
Kaimook.

71
00:07:59,720 --> 00:08:00,680
Kaimook.

72
00:08:13,880 --> 00:08:15,319
Are you okay?

73
00:08:15,320 --> 00:08:17,160
Did they hurt you?

74
00:08:17,920 --> 00:08:19,760
No. I'm perfectly fine.

75
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:22,400
Thon was really worried about you.

76
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:24,400
In all the years I've been with him,

77
00:08:25,040 --> 00:08:26,199
I've never seen him

78
00:08:26,200 --> 00:08:27,840
worry about anyone this much.

79
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:38,599
You two are probably wondering

80
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:40,320
why this happened.

81
00:08:41,159 --> 00:08:43,720
It's because I discovered
that Sairung murdered Sarai.

82
00:08:47,520 --> 00:08:48,800
You...

83
00:08:49,840 --> 00:08:51,240
know?

84
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,880
You say that as if you already knew.

85
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:55,960
We did.

86
00:08:58,440 --> 00:08:59,519
Ms. Sarai's spirit

87
00:08:59,520 --> 00:09:02,000
tried to contact my friend Da
and asked for help.

88
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:04,679
But it wasn't until recently

89
00:09:04,680 --> 00:09:06,439
that we realized the spirit

90
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:08,080
was actually Ms. Sarai.

91
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:12,600
Sarai must have suffered terribly.

92
00:09:15,120 --> 00:09:17,080
I didn't tell you earlier

93
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:19,400
because

94
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:21,160
I misunderstood.

95
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:25,239
I thought you were

96
00:09:25,240 --> 00:09:27,960
involved in her death.

97
00:09:29,640 --> 00:09:31,080
I'm sorry.

98
00:09:33,600 --> 00:09:34,760
You're not the only one.

99
00:09:35,640 --> 00:09:37,400
By the time Sarai learned the truth,

100
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:40,640
she'd already put me in the hospital.

101
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:45,600
You've met Sarai's spirit?

102
00:09:49,360 --> 00:09:50,680
Then where is she now?

103
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,360
What are you doing, Kang?

104
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,760
Please allow me to mop the floor.

105
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:08,599
It's alright. I'll do it.

106
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:10,479
Please trust me.

107
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:13,159
The temple is much bigger than this room,

108
00:10:13,160 --> 00:10:15,279
and I cleaned it perfectly.

109
00:10:15,280 --> 00:10:17,039
Venerable Sir said himself that

110
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:18,439
if a fly landed on the floor,

111
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:20,440
it would definitely slip.

112
00:10:21,880 --> 00:10:23,040
Alright.

113
00:10:28,640 --> 00:10:30,360
What?

114
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:33,400
You heard me correctly.

115
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:39,360
Sarai's spirit is now
inside Pakarang's body.

116
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:43,440
To put it simply,
Pakarang has become Sarai's new body.

117
00:10:45,280 --> 00:10:46,880
Who exactly is Pakarang?

118
00:10:48,160 --> 00:10:50,240
How can Sarai use her body?

119
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:57,080
Stop trying. She's dead.

120
00:11:02,480 --> 00:11:03,560
She's awake!

121
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:12,519
Can Ms. Sarai continue living

122
00:11:12,520 --> 00:11:14,480
in someone else's body forever?

123
00:11:15,760 --> 00:11:19,280
Pakarang's body is still a dead body.
It will continue to deteriorate.

124
00:11:19,800 --> 00:11:21,919
That's why she sometimes

125
00:11:21,920 --> 00:11:23,639
becomes extremely weak,

126
00:11:23,640 --> 00:11:25,680
pale, and exhausted.

127
00:11:28,680 --> 00:11:30,200
Then how does she recover?

128
00:11:31,760 --> 00:11:34,000
She needs blood to preserve the body.

129
00:11:35,240 --> 00:11:36,800
Like a vampire?

130
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:40,719
Then does that mean

131
00:11:40,720 --> 00:11:42,959
Sarai has to kill people

132
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:44,880
just to survive?

133
00:11:46,560 --> 00:11:49,000
She had no choice but to kill
those two teenagers

134
00:11:49,720 --> 00:11:51,319
because they tried to assault her

135
00:11:51,320 --> 00:11:53,720
when her body was at its weakest.

136
00:11:57,320 --> 00:11:58,840
But I already solved the problem

137
00:11:59,360 --> 00:12:01,559
by buying blood from the blood bank

138
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:03,240
at a hospital owned by a friend of mine.

139
00:12:03,920 --> 00:12:06,400
That way, Sarai wouldn't
have to commit any more sins.

140
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:10,280
Thon.

141
00:12:11,280 --> 00:12:13,400
There's something else I need to tell you.

142
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:15,440
What is it?

143
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:19,240
Sarai and I had a child together.

144
00:12:20,720 --> 00:12:22,480
But he's missing.

145
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:25,160
I already know.

146
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,240
You're not angry?

147
00:12:31,120 --> 00:12:32,120
Not at all.

148
00:12:34,160 --> 00:12:37,040
I'll help you find my brother.

149
00:12:50,480 --> 00:12:52,239
Thank you.

150
00:12:52,240 --> 00:12:53,560
Thank you so much.

151
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:33,160
Why did you bring me back to this temple?

152
00:13:34,920 --> 00:13:36,760
We're going to hide here for a while.

153
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:40,560
You can stay here by yourself.
I'm going somewhere else.

154
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:42,400
Do you have any money?

155
00:13:44,400 --> 00:13:45,879
Thongdee was smart.

156
00:13:45,880 --> 00:13:46,999
He became a monk

157
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,799
and hid here for years.

158
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:50,120
Nobody ever suspected him.

159
00:13:50,720 --> 00:13:52,640
That's why
this is the safest place possible.

160
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:55,000
What are you saying?

161
00:13:55,560 --> 00:13:57,079
Are you planning to become a monk?

162
00:13:57,080 --> 00:13:58,079
And what about me?

163
00:13:58,080 --> 00:14:00,359
I'm a woman.
Am I supposed to become a nun?

164
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:01,759
Don't be stupid.

165
00:14:01,760 --> 00:14:03,760
We can stay here
under some other pretense.

166
00:14:04,360 --> 00:14:07,040
Thongdee's the abbot.
He'll be able to arrange something.

167
00:14:08,600 --> 00:14:10,120
And what if he refuses to help us?

168
00:14:14,640 --> 00:14:15,640
He won't dare.

169
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:18,320
We're all in the same boat.

170
00:14:18,920 --> 00:14:20,640
If we go down, he goes down too.

171
00:14:21,160 --> 00:14:23,039
Trust me.

172
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:24,879
This is the safest place.

173
00:14:24,880 --> 00:14:27,120
More importantly,
it won't cost us a single baht.

174
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:30,079
Let's say

175
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:31,920
we'll stay here

176
00:14:32,560 --> 00:14:34,160
until we come up with another plan.

177
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:47,480
He left the monkhood?

178
00:14:48,200 --> 00:14:49,400
Since when?

179
00:14:51,240 --> 00:14:53,120
Come on. Walk slowly.

180
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:56,960
I don't know what happened.

181
00:14:57,960 --> 00:14:59,440
He doesn't look good.

182
00:15:01,360 --> 00:15:02,599
Be careful of rocks.

183
00:15:02,600 --> 00:15:04,639
Don't trip and fall.

184
00:15:04,640 --> 00:15:05,840
Thongdee?

185
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:09,080
What happened?

186
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:15,399
Slowly.

187
00:15:15,400 --> 00:15:17,200
Watch his head.

188
00:15:24,280 --> 00:15:26,279
Put his hands down properly.

189
00:15:26,280 --> 00:15:28,080
He can't breathe.

190
00:15:29,040 --> 00:15:30,280
Why is Thong...

191
00:15:30,960 --> 00:15:32,520
I mean, why is he in this condition?

192
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:34,879
I don't know.

193
00:15:34,880 --> 00:15:36,999
He suddenly disappeared from the temple

194
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:39,720
and left the monkhood
without telling anyone.

195
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:41,239
Good thing

196
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:43,039
earlier today, some temple boys

197
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:45,160
went to collect mushrooms near the woods

198
00:15:45,760 --> 00:15:46,999
and found him unconscious.

199
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:48,960
So they brought him back here.

200
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:54,359
And

201
00:15:54,360 --> 00:15:56,320
who are you two?

202
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:58,080
What brings you here?

203
00:16:01,520 --> 00:16:02,759
We're

204
00:16:02,760 --> 00:16:05,040
relatives of his.

205
00:16:05,880 --> 00:16:07,160
We just happened to stop by to visit him.

206
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:08,960
Relatives?

207
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:14,080
Good then.

208
00:16:14,880 --> 00:16:16,239
In that case,

209
00:16:16,240 --> 00:16:18,519
please look after him.

210
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:20,799
The monks and I

211
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:22,919
have been invited to perform funeral rites

212
00:16:22,920 --> 00:16:25,080
in the neighboring village.

213
00:16:26,200 --> 00:16:28,039
It's too late

214
00:16:28,040 --> 00:16:29,400
to cancel now.

215
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:31,120
Alright?

216
00:16:32,440 --> 00:16:35,559
Of course. I'll take care of him.

217
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:36,480
Please go ahead.

218
00:16:37,640 --> 00:16:40,520
If you need anything,
call the temple boys.

219
00:16:42,120 --> 00:16:43,399
Let's go.

220
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:45,439
We're going to be late.

221
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:46,760
Hurry up.

222
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:18,800
What's going on?

223
00:17:23,400 --> 00:17:24,800
Sarai.

224
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:32,640
They know everything now.

225
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:38,440
I'm so happy

226
00:17:39,720 --> 00:17:41,360
to see you again.

227
00:17:44,800 --> 00:17:47,559
I've missed you too, Mr. Narathon.

228
00:17:47,560 --> 00:17:49,960
You were my best friend.

229
00:17:57,920 --> 00:17:59,240
I'm sorry

230
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:02,120
I didn't understand

231
00:18:02,800 --> 00:18:04,800
when you were trying to ask for help.

232
00:18:06,280 --> 00:18:09,120
You had to suffer for so long.

233
00:18:10,960 --> 00:18:12,160
It's alright.

234
00:18:12,680 --> 00:18:14,520
Perhaps it was my karma.

235
00:18:18,120 --> 00:18:19,400
Ms. Kaimook.

236
00:18:20,160 --> 00:18:21,639
Thank you.

237
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:25,399
If you hadn't freed me
from that coral reef beneath the sea,

238
00:18:25,400 --> 00:18:28,120
I would never have had
the chance to see everyone again.

239
00:18:29,960 --> 00:18:32,039
I should be thanking you too.

240
00:18:32,040 --> 00:18:33,960
You saved my life on Skull Island.

241
00:18:37,720 --> 00:18:39,800
Are we going to stand here
talking forever?

242
00:18:40,320 --> 00:18:42,079
Let's go inside and make something to eat.

243
00:18:42,080 --> 00:18:45,040
We should celebrate being together again.

244
00:18:45,840 --> 00:18:46,840
Sounds great.

245
00:18:47,640 --> 00:18:49,600
I just realized I'm starving.

246
00:18:51,600 --> 00:18:53,000
Sarai,

247
00:18:53,720 --> 00:18:55,039
can you make fried rice for me?

248
00:18:55,040 --> 00:18:57,360
I've really missed your cooking so much.

249
00:18:58,080 --> 00:19:01,039
Sure. Then let me
show off my cooking skills.

250
00:19:01,040 --> 00:19:03,199
Hold on. Thon,

251
00:19:03,200 --> 00:19:04,559
I'm sorry.

252
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:06,200
I'll cook today.

253
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:10,640
Come help me make fried rice.

254
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,280
Here.

255
00:19:59,600 --> 00:20:00,760
I can't eat this.

256
00:20:01,760 --> 00:20:03,679
Stop being so picky.

257
00:20:03,680 --> 00:20:06,200
Just eat. Staying alive comes first.

258
00:20:08,560 --> 00:20:09,960
Kang...

259
00:20:11,480 --> 00:20:12,720
Kang.

260
00:20:21,040 --> 00:20:22,360
Kang.

261
00:20:23,400 --> 00:20:24,680
Who is he calling?

262
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:29,000
Probably

263
00:20:29,760 --> 00:20:31,640
that temple boy we met before.

264
00:20:36,400 --> 00:20:37,720
Sarai.

265
00:20:39,680 --> 00:20:40,840
Sarai.

266
00:20:44,720 --> 00:20:45,800
Check him.

267
00:20:55,160 --> 00:20:56,400
He's burning up.

268
00:20:57,040 --> 00:20:58,160
Must be a fever.

269
00:20:58,760 --> 00:21:01,840
Why is he rambling
about Sarai and that boy?

270
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:03,920
How would I know?

271
00:21:04,960 --> 00:21:07,439
Kang, Kang.

272
00:21:07,440 --> 00:21:09,040
Sarai.

273
00:21:09,920 --> 00:21:11,320
Please forgive me.

274
00:21:13,840 --> 00:21:15,440
Sarai? Kang?

275
00:21:16,120 --> 00:21:17,720
Forgive?

276
00:21:24,160 --> 00:21:26,160
You're thinking
the same thing I am, aren't you?

277
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,960
Please forgive me.

278
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,320
Forgive me.

279
00:21:45,880 --> 00:21:47,799
Kang, get me some eggs.

280
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:48,800
Yes.

281
00:21:50,880 --> 00:21:52,720
How many do you want?

282
00:21:53,320 --> 00:21:55,240
Just as many as you want.

283
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:57,240
How about you, ma'am?

284
00:21:57,880 --> 00:21:58,999
Up to you.

285
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:01,240
Then I'll get six.

286
00:22:08,840 --> 00:22:10,159
Alright.

287
00:22:10,160 --> 00:22:11,920
Here you go.

288
00:22:14,760 --> 00:22:16,239
How many are there?

289
00:22:16,240 --> 00:22:17,919
Six.

290
00:22:17,920 --> 00:22:20,360
You got six?

291
00:22:21,160 --> 00:22:22,199
Wow.

292
00:22:22,200 --> 00:22:23,920
Kang is so adorable.

293
00:22:25,280 --> 00:22:27,279
Watching them, it feels like
a father, mother, and child

294
00:22:27,280 --> 00:22:29,520
cooking together.

295
00:22:30,680 --> 00:22:32,960
You seem to love children.

296
00:22:34,240 --> 00:22:36,080
I do. I like children.

297
00:22:36,680 --> 00:22:39,280
They're cute and innocent.

298
00:22:39,960 --> 00:22:41,600
Being around them makes me happy.

299
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:45,960
Good.

300
00:22:46,960 --> 00:22:48,400
I love children too.

301
00:22:50,280 --> 00:22:53,040
Our home in the future should be lively.

302
00:22:56,440 --> 00:22:57,640
What?

303
00:22:58,760 --> 00:23:01,840
I mean our future children.

304
00:23:06,720 --> 00:23:10,360
You really know how to turn
everything back to yourself, don't you?

305
00:23:12,600 --> 00:23:15,200
Who said it's about me?

306
00:23:15,800 --> 00:23:17,880
It's about us.

307
00:23:23,320 --> 00:23:25,879
I'm not talking to you anymore.

308
00:23:25,880 --> 00:23:27,760
I'll go help Ms. Sarai.

309
00:23:30,720 --> 00:23:32,200
It's done.

310
00:23:34,440 --> 00:23:36,239
Is there anything I can help with?

311
00:23:36,240 --> 00:23:38,479
We're just about done.

312
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:40,600
- Could you help set the table?
- Okay.

313
00:24:03,120 --> 00:24:04,759
Thank you for driving me.

314
00:24:04,760 --> 00:24:06,999
I could have just driven myself back.

315
00:24:07,000 --> 00:24:08,520
It's alright.

316
00:24:09,240 --> 00:24:10,520
I wanted to.

317
00:24:14,160 --> 00:24:16,880
Thank you for today.

318
00:24:20,080 --> 00:24:20,960
It's alright.

319
00:24:23,200 --> 00:24:25,120
If you hadn't suggested that I come home,

320
00:24:26,720 --> 00:24:27,800
I wouldn't

321
00:24:28,440 --> 00:24:29,920
have made it in time to save Dad.

322
00:24:32,640 --> 00:24:33,760
It's alright.

323
00:24:34,280 --> 00:24:35,559
I'm just glad

324
00:24:35,560 --> 00:24:38,360
everything worked out for the best.

325
00:24:40,200 --> 00:24:41,960
Seeing you and Mr. Phum

326
00:24:42,560 --> 00:24:43,680
finally understand each other

327
00:24:44,440 --> 00:24:45,960
makes me happy too.

328
00:24:55,080 --> 00:24:56,240
Wait, Kaimook.

329
00:25:00,560 --> 00:25:01,440
Yes?

330
00:25:20,880 --> 00:25:22,160
This was my mother's ring.

331
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:25,560
I've worn it for a long time.

332
00:25:28,080 --> 00:25:30,960
I always intended to give it
to the person I love most.

333
00:25:34,720 --> 00:25:36,239
And now,

334
00:25:36,240 --> 00:25:38,000
I think I've found her.

335
00:25:41,800 --> 00:25:43,560
Mr. Narathon...

336
00:25:47,440 --> 00:25:49,240
It wouldn't be appropriate for me

337
00:25:49,960 --> 00:25:51,600
to put it on your finger right now.

338
00:25:54,240 --> 00:25:56,359
So may I ask you

339
00:25:56,360 --> 00:25:58,720
to keep it with you like this for now?

340
00:26:12,920 --> 00:26:15,000
I probably...

341
00:26:18,600 --> 00:26:20,000
You can't accept it?

342
00:26:22,080 --> 00:26:23,960
Does that mean
you're still unsure about me?

343
00:26:30,160 --> 00:26:32,880
I was going to say
I probably can't refuse it.

344
00:27:05,440 --> 00:27:07,399
I'll take the best care

345
00:27:07,400 --> 00:27:08,920
of this ring.

346
00:27:10,200 --> 00:27:11,080
Thank you.

347
00:27:42,800 --> 00:27:45,760
I'll go inside now.

348
00:27:46,440 --> 00:27:47,400
Alright.

349
00:28:19,600 --> 00:28:20,720
Did you find out anything?

350
00:28:21,240 --> 00:28:23,080
It's exactly what we thought.

351
00:28:24,600 --> 00:28:26,200
When Thongdee came here to become a monk,

352
00:28:26,760 --> 00:28:28,160
he brought a baby with him.

353
00:28:28,680 --> 00:28:31,239
He told everyone

354
00:28:31,240 --> 00:28:33,800
it was his late sister's child.

355
00:28:35,200 --> 00:28:36,639
And how can you be sure

356
00:28:36,640 --> 00:28:39,280
that child is Sarai's?

357
00:28:39,960 --> 00:28:41,880
Thongdee doesn't have any siblings.

358
00:28:45,640 --> 00:28:47,120
That boy Kang

359
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:51,240
has to be Sarai's missing child.

360
00:28:53,800 --> 00:28:54,920
Luck is on our side.

361
00:28:56,920 --> 00:28:58,040
What are you going to do?

362
00:28:59,760 --> 00:29:02,000
Kidnap him and demand ransom.

363
00:29:03,200 --> 00:29:04,479
Do you know

364
00:29:04,480 --> 00:29:06,640
where that boy is?

365
00:29:07,800 --> 00:29:10,200
The temple boys said Thongdee

366
00:29:11,120 --> 00:29:13,360
recently sent him
to live with Mr. Narathon.

367
00:29:15,160 --> 00:29:16,200
What?

368
00:29:19,120 --> 00:29:22,039
Thongdee must be trying

369
00:29:22,040 --> 00:29:23,599
to return the child to your husband

370
00:29:23,600 --> 00:29:25,200
to redeem himself.

371
00:29:28,600 --> 00:29:29,959
But Mr. Phum

372
00:29:29,960 --> 00:29:31,920
never said anything about this.

373
00:29:32,640 --> 00:29:36,400
That means your husband and everyone
still don't know Kang is his son.

374
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:38,479
So, it's the best opportunity for us

375
00:29:38,480 --> 00:29:40,960
to kidnap him.

376
00:29:41,560 --> 00:29:43,119
But you saw it yourself.

377
00:29:43,120 --> 00:29:45,920
Kang wasn't at Mr. Phum's house.

378
00:29:48,560 --> 00:29:50,360
They probably left him
somewhere else first

379
00:29:51,040 --> 00:29:52,320
so they could deal with you.

380
00:29:56,360 --> 00:29:57,559
Anyway,

381
00:29:57,560 --> 00:29:59,320
does your husband have another place?

382
00:30:00,840 --> 00:30:02,199
He has a condo.

383
00:30:02,200 --> 00:30:04,200
But he let Pakarang stay there.

384
00:30:07,000 --> 00:30:07,880
Wait.

385
00:30:08,560 --> 00:30:09,440
Or maybe...

386
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:43,640
Oh.

387
00:30:44,880 --> 00:30:47,199
I only went downstairs
to see Thon and Kaimook off for a moment,

388
00:30:47,200 --> 00:30:48,839
and he's already fast asleep.

389
00:30:48,840 --> 00:30:50,120
Kids will be kids.

390
00:30:51,120 --> 00:30:52,480
He must be tired.

391
00:30:53,000 --> 00:30:54,439
He's very hardworking.

392
00:30:54,440 --> 00:30:56,680
He helped me clean the room all day today.

393
00:30:58,440 --> 00:30:59,280
Alright.

394
00:31:00,960 --> 00:31:02,639
Where are you taking him?

395
00:31:02,640 --> 00:31:03,919
Oh?

396
00:31:03,920 --> 00:31:05,800
We are all going home together.

397
00:31:07,720 --> 00:31:10,199
Let him sleep here with me tonight.

398
00:31:10,200 --> 00:31:11,759
I haven't packed anything yet.

399
00:31:11,760 --> 00:31:13,840
I didn't expect you
to come for me this quickly.

400
00:31:16,280 --> 00:31:18,360
I don't want to be away from you anymore,.

401
00:31:21,720 --> 00:31:23,120
It's only one night.

402
00:31:23,720 --> 00:31:26,040
You can come pick me and Kang up tomorrow.

403
00:31:26,800 --> 00:31:28,240
I'll be ready.

404
00:31:37,520 --> 00:31:40,080
Do you know how much it tortures me

405
00:31:41,760 --> 00:31:43,880
to be so close to you...

406
00:31:46,120 --> 00:31:47,680
and yet only be able to hold you?

407
00:31:54,960 --> 00:31:56,440
Mr. Phum...

408
00:32:00,960 --> 00:32:02,760
Because this body isn't yours.

409
00:32:12,880 --> 00:32:14,960
We can touch each other with our hearts.

410
00:32:17,040 --> 00:32:18,080
Forever.

411
00:32:59,560 --> 00:33:00,600
<i>Da.</i>

412
00:33:01,560 --> 00:33:02,719
<i>Da.</i>

413
00:33:02,720 --> 00:33:04,160
<i>Help me.</i>

414
00:33:06,840 --> 00:33:07,920
<i>Da!</i>

415
00:33:08,840 --> 00:33:10,080
<i>Help me!</i>

416
00:34:27,760 --> 00:34:28,880
Da.

417
00:34:30,360 --> 00:34:31,719
Help me, Da.

418
00:34:33,280 --> 00:34:34,120
Da.

419
00:34:34,679 --> 00:34:35,760
Help me.

420
00:34:36,639 --> 00:34:38,960
Da, help me.

421
00:34:39,600 --> 00:34:40,439
Win!

422
00:34:40,440 --> 00:34:41,600
Da!

423
00:34:42,520 --> 00:34:43,679
Help me!

424
00:35:05,320 --> 00:35:06,360
Skull island?

425
00:35:14,280 --> 00:35:15,280
This is not true.

426
00:35:16,080 --> 00:35:17,960
This is not true. It's impossible.

427
00:35:18,840 --> 00:35:19,800
It's not true.

428
00:35:20,840 --> 00:35:21,840
It's not true.

429
00:35:22,520 --> 00:35:26,079
It's not true!

430
00:35:26,080 --> 00:35:27,480
No!

431
00:35:53,640 --> 00:35:54,800
Da.

432
00:35:58,400 --> 00:35:59,600
Are you alright?

433
00:36:00,200 --> 00:36:02,840
You didn't sound good
when you called this morning.

434
00:36:03,960 --> 00:36:05,680
What happened, Da?

435
00:36:10,960 --> 00:36:13,200
Last night, I had
a really terrifying dream about Win.

436
00:36:13,920 --> 00:36:15,360
I called him, but he didn't answer.

437
00:36:18,160 --> 00:36:19,000
Mook,

438
00:36:19,720 --> 00:36:22,120
I'm afraid something happened to him.

439
00:36:24,440 --> 00:36:25,999
Come on, Da.

440
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:27,800
It was just a dream.

441
00:36:39,200 --> 00:36:41,720
Da, if you're worried,

442
00:36:42,480 --> 00:36:44,680
let's go see him at his condo.

443
00:36:56,120 --> 00:36:57,880
How was it? Did you find him?

444
00:36:59,280 --> 00:37:00,320
No.

445
00:37:02,320 --> 00:37:03,719
This is strange.

446
00:37:03,720 --> 00:37:05,400
Where did he go?

447
00:37:06,760 --> 00:37:09,280
How long has it been
since Win last contacted you?

448
00:37:11,120 --> 00:37:12,960
Normally, we don't talk that often,

449
00:37:13,720 --> 00:37:16,320
so I wouldn't have thought he was missing

450
00:37:17,880 --> 00:37:19,719
if I hadn't

451
00:37:19,720 --> 00:37:22,480
had that terrifying dream
about him last night.

452
00:37:23,360 --> 00:37:24,840
What did you dream about?

453
00:37:26,240 --> 00:37:27,520
I saw Win

454
00:37:28,280 --> 00:37:30,600
looking terrible,

455
00:37:31,680 --> 00:37:33,360
asking me to help him.

456
00:37:39,200 --> 00:37:42,320
People say bad dreams
turn into good fortune, Da.

457
00:37:44,520 --> 00:37:46,800
But this time,
I have a really strange feeling.

458
00:37:47,520 --> 00:37:49,440
I've never felt like this before.

459
00:37:54,400 --> 00:37:56,239
Could you be overthinking it?

460
00:37:56,240 --> 00:37:58,559
Maybe Win is with his girlfriend,

461
00:37:58,560 --> 00:38:00,760
the one you told me about.

462
00:38:02,560 --> 00:38:03,800
You mean Pat?

463
00:38:06,280 --> 00:38:07,799
That's possible.

464
00:38:07,800 --> 00:38:09,080
Do you have her number?

465
00:38:09,640 --> 00:38:10,680
Try calling her.

466
00:38:11,920 --> 00:38:13,119
No.

467
00:38:13,120 --> 00:38:15,320
I only know she works in event organizing.

468
00:38:17,320 --> 00:38:18,599
Organizing?

469
00:38:18,600 --> 00:38:20,439
I know a Pat

470
00:38:20,440 --> 00:38:22,160
who works in event organizing too.

471
00:38:23,480 --> 00:38:24,480
I have a photo of her.

472
00:38:27,480 --> 00:38:29,440
Win once sent it to me.

473
00:38:30,280 --> 00:38:31,600
Let's see.

474
00:38:37,400 --> 00:38:38,800
Ms. Pat.

475
00:38:40,280 --> 00:38:41,880
Is she the same person you know?

476
00:38:44,720 --> 00:38:46,079
Mook,

477
00:38:46,080 --> 00:38:48,720
then do you know where she lives or works?

478
00:38:50,840 --> 00:38:53,000
Ms. Pat lives at Mr. Phum's condominium.

479
00:39:02,960 --> 00:39:04,559
Just as you saw,

480
00:39:04,560 --> 00:39:06,679
no one was in the room.

481
00:39:06,680 --> 00:39:08,839
Besides, the housekeepers said

482
00:39:08,840 --> 00:39:11,000
Ms. Pat hasn't returned for several days.

483
00:39:13,600 --> 00:39:14,920
Thank you.

484
00:39:15,520 --> 00:39:17,880
Excuse me then.

485
00:39:20,640 --> 00:39:22,640
- Oh?
- Oh, Mr. Narathon.

486
00:39:23,280 --> 00:39:24,640
What are you all doing here?

487
00:39:26,280 --> 00:39:27,800
We're looking for Ms. Pat.

488
00:39:29,200 --> 00:39:30,840
Is it about the gallery?

489
00:39:32,080 --> 00:39:33,319
No.

490
00:39:33,320 --> 00:39:34,599
Win,

491
00:39:34,600 --> 00:39:36,400
Da's brother, has gone missing.

492
00:39:40,840 --> 00:39:42,399
It's a long story.

493
00:39:42,400 --> 00:39:44,239
We're going to get some coffee.

494
00:39:44,240 --> 00:39:45,720
Care to join us, Mr. Narathon?

495
00:39:47,200 --> 00:39:48,080
Of course.

496
00:39:48,760 --> 00:39:51,120
Maybe there's something I can help with.

497
00:39:53,200 --> 00:39:54,400
Thank you.

498
00:39:56,520 --> 00:39:58,399
It's alright.

499
00:39:58,400 --> 00:40:00,320
You've helped me a lot, Ms. Da.

500
00:40:04,200 --> 00:40:05,159
Shall we go now?

501
00:40:05,160 --> 00:40:06,279
Wait.

502
00:40:06,280 --> 00:40:08,800
Weren't you here
to see Ms. Pakarang and Kang?

503
00:40:10,880 --> 00:40:13,040
Dad will be picking them up
and taking them home soon.

504
00:40:14,040 --> 00:40:15,600
I can meet them at home later.

505
00:40:19,640 --> 00:40:20,879
Shall we go?

506
00:40:20,880 --> 00:40:22,000
Let's go.

507
00:40:28,160 --> 00:40:29,760
That looks so delicious.

508
00:40:30,360 --> 00:40:32,799
I've never had breakfast like this before.

509
00:40:32,800 --> 00:40:33,719
Really?

510
00:40:33,720 --> 00:40:35,199
Yes.

511
00:40:35,200 --> 00:40:37,440
Then what do you usually eat, Kang?

512
00:40:38,040 --> 00:40:40,040
The food Venerable Sir receives
in his alms bowl.

513
00:40:41,360 --> 00:40:42,959
Then,

514
00:40:42,960 --> 00:40:44,399
you have to finish all of it, okay?

515
00:40:44,400 --> 00:40:45,600
Yes.

516
00:40:49,120 --> 00:40:51,400
Oh dear, we're out of ketchup.

517
00:40:52,400 --> 00:40:55,000
You need it for the eggs and sausages.

518
00:40:55,840 --> 00:40:59,000
I haven't been here for several days,
so I didn't notice what had run out.

519
00:40:59,880 --> 00:41:02,039
It's okay. I can eat it.

520
00:41:02,040 --> 00:41:03,199
No, dear.

521
00:41:03,200 --> 00:41:05,760
It's much tastier with ketchup.

522
00:41:07,960 --> 00:41:08,999
How about this?

523
00:41:09,000 --> 00:41:10,679
I'll go buy some.

524
00:41:10,680 --> 00:41:13,159
There's a convenience store downstairs.
Just wait here for a moment, okay?

525
00:41:13,160 --> 00:41:14,120
Okay.

526
00:41:57,240 --> 00:41:58,600
Auntie's back.

527
00:42:11,280 --> 00:42:12,960
Who are you here for?

528
00:42:45,040 --> 00:42:45,880
Sarai.

529
00:42:46,640 --> 00:42:48,759
Mr. Phum, you're here so early.

530
00:42:48,760 --> 00:42:49,999
Have you had breakfast yet?

531
00:42:50,000 --> 00:42:52,799
Not yet. I wanted
to have breakfast with you and Kang.

532
00:42:52,800 --> 00:42:53,799
Where's Kang?

533
00:42:53,800 --> 00:42:54,960
He's waiting upstairs.

534
00:42:56,000 --> 00:42:57,080
Let's go.

535
00:43:03,560 --> 00:43:05,799
If you cry for help,

536
00:43:05,800 --> 00:43:07,000
you're dead.

537
00:43:08,000 --> 00:43:09,120
Understand?

538
00:43:12,720 --> 00:43:14,080
Understand?

539
00:43:33,560 --> 00:43:35,280
The ketchup's here, Kang.

540
00:43:36,760 --> 00:43:37,760
Kang?

541
00:43:39,040 --> 00:43:40,000
Kang?

542
00:43:40,920 --> 00:43:41,920
Kang?

543
00:43:42,440 --> 00:43:43,520
Where did Kang go?

544
00:43:44,440 --> 00:43:46,120
Maybe he's in the bathroom.

545
00:43:46,640 --> 00:43:48,200
Kang, ketchup's here.

546
00:43:50,640 --> 00:43:51,680
Kang.

547
00:43:53,840 --> 00:43:55,040
He isn't in the bathroom.

548
00:43:58,400 --> 00:44:01,280
Kang.

549
00:44:02,200 --> 00:44:03,600
He's not in the bedroom either.

550
00:44:14,160 --> 00:44:15,400
Where did Kang go?

551
00:44:27,840 --> 00:44:28,800
Give me back my son!

552
00:44:31,040 --> 00:44:32,800
- You're going to die!
- I'm scared.

553
00:44:33,680 --> 00:44:35,199
Kang is your son.

554
00:44:35,200 --> 00:44:36,520
My son...

555
00:44:37,360 --> 00:44:38,319
My son.

556
00:44:38,320 --> 00:44:41,520
I'm glad you've finally learned the truth.

557
00:45:12,680 --> 00:45:14,920
Subtitle translation by: Panuwat Baikeawon
